{
  "title": "Modified store useCartStore to merge repeated items",
  "context": [
    "A shopper who added the same product twice got two lines for that product in the cart. The cart now keeps one line per product, and each further add raises the quantity of that line by one. The cart count in the header and the cart total stay the same.",
    "",
    "## Overview",
    "",
    "- **When** a shopper clicks \"Add to cart\" on a product that is already in the cart, **then** [the cart keeps one line for the product and adds 1 to its quantity](code:src/stores/cart-store.ts#L17-21).",
    "- **When** a shopper clicks \"Add to cart\" on a product that is not in the cart, **then** nothing changes.",
    "- **When** a shopper opens the cart after two adds of one product, **then** the cart page shows one line that reads \"2 items\" with the price of two, where it showed two lines of \"1 item\". `CartLine` in `src/routes/cart/components/CartLine.tsx` renders the line.",
    "- **When** a shopper reads the cart count in the header or the cart total, **then** nothing changes.",
    "- **When** a shopper clicks \"Remove\" on a product that was added twice, **then** nothing changes.",
    "",
    "## Implementation",
    "",
    "**`src/stores/cart-store.ts`**",
    "",
    "- Modified [the `addItem` function of `useCartStore`](code:src/stores/cart-store.ts#L13-23) to add 1 to the `quantity` of the item with the same `product.id`, and to append `{ product, quantity: 1 }` only when `items` holds no such item."
  ],
  "diff": [
    "diff --git a/src/stores/cart-store.ts b/src/stores/cart-store.ts",
    "--- a/src/stores/cart-store.ts",
    "+++ b/src/stores/cart-store.ts",
    "@@ -14 +14,9 @@ export const useCartStore = create<CartState>((set) => ({",
    "-    set((state) => ({ items: [...state.items, { product, quantity: 1 }] }))",
    "+    set((state) => {",
    "+      const isInCart = state.items.some((item) => item.product.id === product.id)",
    "+      if (!isInCart) return { items: [...state.items, { product, quantity: 1 }] }",
    "+      return {",
    "+        items: state.items.map((item) =>",
    "+          item.product.id === product.id ? { ...item, quantity: item.quantity + 1 } : item,",
    "+        ),",
    "+      }",
    "+    })"
  ],
